<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Baltic Fury #3 - Warsaw Uprising, 1994</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Baltic Fury 3 Warsaw Uprising! 1994&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;18 Feb 1994.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is the third scenario of a 5-scenario campaign. Baltic Fury is very closely linked to the Northern Fury campaign. You can explore the situation on the &lt;A href="http://northernfury.bhgdesigns.com/index.php" target=_BLANK&gt;webpage&lt;/A&gt; read the Northern Fury background document for further insight. The key nuggets&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Cold War continued, no thaw in relations. Germany is unified but somewhat unstable, the Warsaw Pact (WP) still active but somewhat less of a force than it was in the 1980s&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;On 11 Feb 1994 there was a bloody coup in Warsaw setting off a complex set of dominos in that country. Hard liners seized power from the struggling reformist Solidarity government and rejoined the Warsaw Treaty Organization commonly known as the Warsaw Pact (WP), which it had left three years earlier. Security force clashes with pro-solidarity/western factions throughout the country flared up in many areas and civil disobedience was widespread.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Global war started on 13 Feb with massive surprise attacks around the world. In the Baltic a fierce air and naval campaign was started with heavy casualties on both sides. The Soviets, lacking immediate access to bases in Poland and the former East Germany were at an initial disadvantage which they mitigated by reinforcing the 15&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Air Army and the Air Arm of the Baltic Fleet with several regiments of aircraft from the Moscow Military District Air Army, some of these have now been withdrawn or redeployed.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The Soviets have seized Bornholm Island and established sea and air dominance over the Eastern Baltic. They are using an expanding presence on Bornholm and on Polish bases to exert increasing pressure on Germany and Denmark in the Western Baltic.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;On the ground in Europe, Soviet forces initially attacked west out of Czechoslovakia towards the Fulda Gap, making limited headway with another thrust north by 20&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Gds Army to threaten Berlin. Yesterday, 17 Feb, saw a massive and confusing battle in the Leipzig area with major elements, probably from 3&lt;SUP&gt;rd&lt;/SUP&gt; Shock Army attacking northwestward into the flank of III German and the advancing I British Corps.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;&lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/warsaw/pl/" target=_BLANK&gt;Polish forces&lt;/A&gt; are mobilizing slowly. &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/warsaw/pl/airforce/" target=_BLANK&gt;Air forces&lt;/A&gt; have responded quickly to mobilization and sits at about 75% of its planned strength. The &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/warsaw/pl/navy/" target=_BLANK&gt;Navy&lt;/A&gt; has had mixed returns, some ships are already deployed but there are stories of a brutally squashed mutiny aboard an Osa Class missile boat and several others having major maintenance faults limiting their ability to put to sea. The &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/warsaw/pl/army/" target=_BLANK&gt;Army&lt;/A&gt; has dispersed the 1&lt;SUP&gt;st&lt;/SUP&gt; Combined Arms Army (CAA) into forward tactical positions largely as anticipated but they have not commenced offensive operations yet, 2&lt;SUP&gt;nd&lt;/SUP&gt; CAA is still in its garrisons and is estimated at about 50% strength – they should have deployed two days ago so are experiencing difficulty. At least one division in 3&lt;SUP&gt;rd&lt;/SUP&gt; CAA has been dissolved, probably to assist the deployment of 1&lt;SUP&gt;st&lt;/SUP&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;You are the commander NATO’s &lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;A href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allied_Forces_Baltic_Approaches" target=_BLANK&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;BALTAP&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt; (Baltic Approaches) Command&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;. BALTAP is a joint force of land, sea and air forces arrayed specifically to keep hostile WP forces bottled up in the Baltic Sea. Your forces are primarily Danish and German reinforced by British and American air forces. The restricted waters in the western Baltic funnel hostile forces directly to the island of Zeeland and Copenhagen itself. Over the past five days the air and sea fight in the central and western Baltic has been withering. Casualties have been high with huge stocks of munitions being expended. Since Bornholm was captured an expanding Soviet presence on that island has forced you to limit your activities to being largely defensive. That is about to change.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Designer’s notes&lt;/STRONG&gt;:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;This is a complex scenario so to assist the player – and to replicate routine operations; there are some missions already in play. The player can choose to use these or delete them as s/he wishes. The No Navigation zones are meant to represent the airspace of Sweden which is restricted and the area controlled by 2&lt;SUP&gt;nd&lt;/SUP&gt; Allied Tactical Air Force (2 ATAF) to your south. 2 ATAF is controlling air forces 8-10 times yours and take a dim view of anyone getting in their way.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You should turn 'special messages' ON, there is quite a bit of information fed to you during the scenario, and you will want to see it. Later in the scenario updates will give you a better idea on what is going on around the world and will give you an idea where subsequent scenarios will lead.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Please respect the initial ready times for aircraft. There are many aircraft with a long ready time, this is to replicate the damage from previous operations, equipment fatigue and general maintenance.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Points are allotted or lost for destruction of air and sea forces as well as completion of tasked missions.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
